Z||000000||theogre||10-12-1999||11:50 AM||||Many of the replacement EGR valves come with a plastic 90 degree fitting on top. The fitting is needed to allow the clearance for the air cleaner.<P>Problem is that the plastic fitting has a nasty habbit of comming off the EGR. This results in a vacuum leak. Even if it doesn't come off or break it can still leak. Quite annoying considering what these things cost.<P>There are 2 fixes you can use. <P>glue the fitting on. be carefull not to let any glue get inside the fitting. You can't use silicones for this, they won't stick to the plastic.<P>replace the fitting and the straight rubber end of the vacuum line with a 90 degree rubber end.<P>If the car is backfireing when you stomp the pedal, check this fitting. then check the rest of the vacuum lines.||||reg||4
